@startuml layer-dependencies

title php-twig-mtier — Layer Dependencies\n(allowed --> and forbidden ..> red)

skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam PackageBorderColor #888888
skinparam defaultFontSize 12

package "Http\\Controller" #FAECE7 {
  [Controllers]
}

package "Service" #FFF2D0 {
  [ServiceFactory]
  [Services]
}

package "Repository" #E1F5EE {
  [Repositories]
}

package "Domain" #FFF8E8 {
  [DomainObjects]
}

package "Infrastructure" #EEEDFE {
  [Database]
}

' === allowed ===
[Controllers]  --> [ServiceFactory] : builds services via
[ServiceFactory] --> [Services]     : constructs
[Controllers]  --> [Services]       : calls
[Controllers]  --> [Repositories]   : calls directly for simple CRUD\n(allowed here — see Design Constraint #4)
[Controllers]  --> [DomainObjects]  : renders
[Services]     --> [Repositories]   : queries / persists
[Services]     --> [DomainObjects]  : uses
[Repositories] --> [DomainObjects]  : hydrates
[Repositories] --> [Database]       : prepared statements
[Services]     --> [Database]       : runInTransaction() only

' === forbidden ===
[Services]      .[#red].> [Controllers]   : FORBIDDEN
[Repositories]  .[#red].> [Services]      : FORBIDDEN
[DomainObjects] .[#red].> [Repositories]  : FORBIDDEN
[DomainObjects] .[#red].> [Services]      : FORBIDDEN
[DomainObjects] .[#red].> [Controllers]   : FORBIDDEN
[Controllers]   .[#red].> [Database]      : FORBIDDEN\n(must go through a Repository)

note bottom of [Controllers]
  The one rule most different from a conventional
  3-tier / DI-container architecture: **web →
  persistence is allowed here**, deliberately, for
  the majority of controllers that need no business
  logic beyond a single repository call.
end note

@enduml
